      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Resolve technical integration and security approach for MVP.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 337175,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Quick update on backend progress. The basic ticket search and creation endpoints for T3 are up and running against the sandbox. I've also got a prototype of the KB search for T6. I've started on the security checklist for T8 and have a draft in A4 for review.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T3",
              "T6",
              "T8",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "fast_forward",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 109718,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "While testing the ticketing integration, I found an issue. The 'get_customer_history' endpoint is very slow and sometimes times out. It's also not well-documented. I've logged this in our tracker A8.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 337175,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "I saw that. Thanks for logging it in A8. Given the 21-day timeline, we might need to reduce scope here. The telephony CTI integration for screen-pops is also looking more complex than we initially thought.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 6869,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "The customer history is a must-have for the MVP. Without it, agents still have to switch screens, which defeats a major purpose of the portal. The CTI screen-pop is a nice-to-have, we can live without it for the pilot.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 109718,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "What if we only pull the last 5 tickets instead of the full history? That might be faster. We'd have to check if the API supports pagination or a limit parameter.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 377231,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "From a UX perspective, showing only 5 tickets with a 'view more' link that might be slow is better than showing nothing. We just need to be transparent with a loading indicator and manage agent expectations.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 561396,
            "reply_to": "M45",
            "text": "So should I build a loading spinner for that panel? What error message should I show if it times out completely?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 337175,
            "reply_to": "M46",
            "text": "Let's make a decision to keep moving. For the MVP, we need to be strict about scope. Proposal for D5: Ticketing integration is limited to ticket search/create and fetching the 5 most recent tickets for a customer. All telephony integration is out of scope for the MVP. Thoughts?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 6869,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "That's a reasonable compromise. The 5 most recent tickets will cover 80% of cases. I agree with that scope for D5.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 109718,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "Agreed. That's technically feasible and reduces our risk significantly.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 377231,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "Works for me. We can design the UI to handle that gracefully.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 561396,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "Ok, I'll build it that way.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 337175,
            "reply_to": "M51",
            "text": "Great, D5 is decided. I'll update the backlog in A3. Now, about security. Please review the checklist in A4 for T8. It covers the main points from the ICT security legislation: auth, data protection, logging.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "A4",
              "T8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M53",
            "speaker_id": 109718,
            "reply_to": "M52",
            "text": "The checklist A4 looks solid. It covers the OWASP top 10 basics. We should schedule a review with the IT security officer next week to get their early feedback.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M54",
            "speaker_id": 6869,
            "reply_to": "M52",
            "text": "I see role-based access is mentioned. That's critical for the KB content management. Looks good to me.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
